.TH CU\-SCANNER 1 "July 2026" "cu\-scanner 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cu\-scanner \- security vulnerability scanning and analysis tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIcsaf\-file\fR]
.br
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR]
[\fB\-D\fR \fIcsaf\-dir\fR]
.br
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR]
\fB\-F\fR
.br
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR]
\fB\-d\fR
.br
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR]
\fB\-\-init\-db\fR
.br
.B cu\-scanner
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-V\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cu\-scanner
is a cybersecurity vulnerability scanning and analysis tool. It processes security advisories in CSAF (Common Security Advisory Framework) format and converts them into OVAL (Open Vulnerability and Assessment Language) XML files.
.PP
Key capabilities:
.IP \(bu 2
Read and parse CSAF security advisory files.
.IP \(bu 2
Convert CSAF advisories into OVAL definitions.
.IP \(bu 2
Save conversion results to a file or print them to standard output.
.IP \(bu 2
Persist OVAL definitions and related data to a PostgreSQL database.
.IP \(bu 2
Batch process CSAF files in a local directory, automatically skipping definitions already present in the database.
.IP \(bu 2
Periodically fetch CSAF indexes from a remote server and synchronize them to the database.
.IP \(bu 2
Run as a daemon providing an HTTP API service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIconfig\-file\fR
Path to the configuration file. Defaults to \fI/etc/cu\-scanner/cu\-scanner.toml\fR. If loading fails, the program falls back to default settings.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-csaf\-file " " \fIcsaf\-file\fR
Path to a single CSAF file to process. The conversion result can be saved via \fB\-o\fR or printed to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-csaf\-dir " " \fIcsaf\-dir\fR
Path to a directory containing CSAF files. The program scans all \fB.json\fR files, extracts an OVAL ID from each filename, skips definitions already in the database, and writes new definitions to the database.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fetch\-csaf
Fetch CSAF files from the network. Requires the \fB[csaf_url]\fR section with a \fBurl\fR value (typically the URL of an \fIindex.txt\fR file). The program parses the index, downloads new advisories in bulk, and converts them.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIoutput\-file\fR
Output path for the OVAL XML result of a single CSAF file conversion. Can only be used with \fB\-f\fR and is incompatible with \fB\-d\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run as an HTTP service daemon. The listen address and port are taken from the \fB[server]\fR section of the configuration file. In daemon mode, if \fB[csaf_url]\fR is configured, a background task periodically fetches CSAF files.
.TP
.BR \-\-init\-db
Initialize the database. The program drops and recreates all tables, then inserts default operating-system information. Ensure the database connection is correctly configured before running this.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH OPERATING MODES
.B cu\-scanner
selects an operating mode based on the command-line arguments. The modes are evaluated in the following priority order:
.PP
.RS
.IP 1. 3
If \fB\-\-init\-db\fR is specified, the program initializes the database and exits.
.IP 2. 3
If \fB\-d\fR is specified, the program enters daemon mode, starts the HTTP service, and starts the periodic CSAF fetch task if configured.
.IP 3. 3
If \fB\-F\fR is specified, the program fetches CSAF files from the network in batch and writes them to the database.
.IP 4. 3
If \fB\-D\fR is specified, the program batch processes CSAF files in a local directory.
.IP 5. 3
If \fB\-f\fR is specified, the program processes a single CSAF file.
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
.B cu\-scanner
uses a TOML configuration file. The default path is \fI/etc/cu\-scanner/cu\-scanner.toml\fR. The file contains the following sections:
.SS [database]
PostgreSQL connection settings used to store OVAL definitions.
.TP
.BR host
Database host address.
.TP
.BR port
Database port; defaults to 5432.
.TP
.BR database
Database name.
.TP
.BR username
Database username.
.TP
.BR password
Database password.
.SS [csaf_url]
Remote CSAF fetch configuration.
.TP
.BR url
URL of the CSAF index file (usually \fIindex.txt\fR).
.TP
.BR fetch_interval_secs
Interval in seconds between periodic CSAF fetches in daemon mode; defaults to 3600 (one hour).
.SS [csaf_db]
CSAF database connection settings used by the network synchronization module.
.SS [logging]
Logging configuration.
.TP
.BR level
Log level; one of \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, or \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.BR file
Log file path, e.g. \fI/var/log/cu\-scanner.log\fR.
.TP
.BR stdout
When set to \fBtrue\fR, logs are written to standard output and \fBfile\fR is ignored.
.SS [api]
API grouping configuration.
.TP
.BR group_name
API route group name; defaults to \fBapi\fR.
.SS [server]
Daemon HTTP service configuration.
.TP
.BR port
Service listen port; defaults to 8093.
.TP
.BR address
Service listen address; defaults to \fB0.0.0.0\fR.
.SS [package]
Package-related configuration.
.TP
.BR epoch_file
Path to the epoch data file, e.g. \fI/etc/cu\-scanner/epoch_data.json\fR.
.TP
.BR use_yum
Whether to use yum as a package source.
.TP
.BR use_extra_yum
Whether to use an additional yum source.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cu\-scanner/cu\-scanner.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/cu\-scanner/epoch_data.json
Default epoch data file.
.TP
.I /var/log/cu\-scanner.log
Default log file path (when \fB[logging].stdout\fR is \fBfalse\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
The examples below assume \fBcu\-scanner\fR is installed in the system PATH. When running from source, replace \fBcu\-scanner\fR with \fBcargo run --bin cu\-scanner --\fR.
.SS Convert a single CSAF file and save to a file
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -f test/csaf/csaf-openeuler-sa-2025-1004.json -o output.xml
.fi
.RE
.SS Convert a single CSAF file to standard output
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -f test/csaf/csaf-openeuler-sa-2025-1004.json
.fi
.RE
.SS Batch process CSAF files in a directory
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -D test/csaf/
.fi
.RE
.SS Batch process with a custom configuration file
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -c /path/to/config.toml -D /path/to/csaf/files/
.fi
.RE
.SS Fetch CSAF files from the network
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -F
.fi
.RE
.SS Initialize the database
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner --init-db
.fi
.RE
.SS Run in daemon mode
.RS
.nf
cu-scanner -d
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B Non-zero
An error occurred, such as a file read failure, database connection failure, or conversion failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B cu\-scanner
requires Rust 1.56 or later. PostgreSQL is optional but required for persistence features.
.SH PROJECT STRUCTURE
.B cu\-scanner
is organized as a Rust workspace. Major modules include:
.TP
.I csaf/
CSAF data structures and processing.
.TP
.I database/
Database operations.
.TP
.I oval/
OVAL data structures and processing.
.TP
.I parser/
CSAF-to-OVAL conversion logic.
.TP
.I utils/
Utility modules, including configuration parsing and logging.
.TP
.I cu\-scanner/
Main program entry point.
.TP
.I networking/
Network service and remote CSAF fetching.
